><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250509110544+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250509110548+10'00'" name="68ff0839-ff2b-4c8f-8fcf-d46e74b5de2f" page="4" coords="49.833664,283.103455,91.971420,283.103455,49.833664,268.335022,91.971420,268.335022" rect="49.372147,267.873505,92.432938,283.564972" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The Xsens Mtw Awinda and the Noraxon MyoMOTION Research Pro MIMUs assessed in this study produced trunk angle measures that can be considered to have acceptable concurrent validity for the tasks assessed, especially for uni-planar ROM movements. Both systems produced RMSDs of less than 3</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-7.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>◦ </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>when compared with 3D retro-reflective motion capture derived angles. Measurement differences during high-speed, multi-planar movements (cricket bowling) were generally greater for both systems, although the RMSDs compared well with previous research. The Xsens system produced RMSDs greater than 5</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-7.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>◦ </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>at various time-points of the bowling delivery stride. It appears varying sensor fusion algorithms and sampling rates can impact MIMU measurement validity. Consumers should be cognizant of discrepancies between commercial MIMU systems when collecting and interpreting data, especially for complex, high-speed movements.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="4" rect="595.276001,191.103455,779.276001,283.103455"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250509110554+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250509110609+10'00'" name="65d2ad0b-4d42-41f4-bc80-ef8a8a2ea224" page="4" coords="49.550720,262.176270,137.511139,262.176270,49.550720,247.415878,137.511139,247.415878" rect="49.089447,246.954605,137.972412,262.637543" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
